WEBVTT

00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:05.200
Hi, this is Dr. Jelena Trajkovic from the CECS Department at Cal State Long Beach.

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:13.200
Let's look at the recap of our binary numbers, and sign binary numbers to be precise.

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:21.060
One thing that we need to notice, and let's start first with the sign and magnitude.

00:00:21.060 --> 00:00:32.640
If we look at the most significant bit, so we will kind of draw a line here.

00:00:32.640 --> 00:00:46.940
Everything above this line starts with 0, both for sine and magnitude, and for two's complement.

00:00:46.940 --> 00:01:10.300
So that applies. Two's complement has positive numbers, starts with 0. Negative numbers are going to start with 1.

00:01:10.300 --> 00:01:21.800
So for sine magnitude, what we can notice is that plus 1 and minus 1 are going to be

00:01:21.800 --> 00:01:26.220
different only in the most significant bit.

00:01:26.220 --> 00:01:33.620
Also plus 2 and minus 2, the only difference is in the most significant bit.

00:01:33.620 --> 00:01:38.100
However, this is a big one.

00:01:38.100 --> 00:01:43.100
plus one is represented as zero, most significant,

00:01:43.740 --> 00:01:46.080
and then zero, zero, one.

00:01:46.080 --> 00:01:49.700
And minus one has completely different presentation.

00:01:49.700 --> 00:01:52.780
One, one, one, one.

00:01:52.780 --> 00:01:55.140
Another thing that is important to see.

00:01:56.700 --> 00:01:58.160
Okay.

00:01:58.160 --> 00:01:59.940
What are the numbers that we can represent

00:01:59.940 --> 00:02:01.920
using a scientist complement?

00:02:02.800 --> 00:02:04.500
We start from plus seven,

00:02:05.760 --> 00:02:08.060
plus six, so and so forth,

00:02:08.060 --> 00:02:11.020
and then we go to zero.

00:02:11.020 --> 00:02:12.780
I'm going to write it as plus zero.

00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:18.960
Then we go into minus one, so and so forth,

00:02:18.960 --> 00:02:21.560
and we go to minus eight.

00:02:21.560 --> 00:02:28.120
So this is plus seven to minus eight

00:02:28.120 --> 00:02:33.120
for two complement counterpart, which is sine magnitude.

00:02:34.400 --> 00:02:37.000
The range is a little bit different.

00:02:37.000 --> 00:02:41.100
we start with plus seven, then we go plus six,

00:02:41.100 --> 00:02:42.060
and so on and so forth.

00:02:42.060 --> 00:02:44.440
And then we have something that is very interesting,

00:02:44.440 --> 00:02:48.240
and that is that we have two representations of zero.

00:02:48.240 --> 00:02:52.800
We have plus zero, then we have minus zero,

00:02:52.800 --> 00:02:55.040
then we have minus one, two, three, and so on and so forth,

00:02:55.040 --> 00:02:56.940
and then we have minus seven.

00:02:58.120 --> 00:03:03.120
So basically, we quote unquote here waste

00:03:03.120 --> 00:03:08.120
one extra number in order to represent minus zero.

00:03:10.840 --> 00:03:15.840
So the range here is plus seven to minus seven.

00:03:17.520 --> 00:03:20.440
In range here, we have one more number

00:03:20.440 --> 00:03:25.440
that we can represent, plus seven up till minus eight.

00:03:27.520 --> 00:03:28.720
Thank you for watching.

